WEBVTT

00:22.949 --> 00:24.826
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:31.851 --> 01:33.812
Drop your weapons now.

01:37.148 --> 01:39.400
Back up and lie on your stomach.

01:39.484 --> 01:42.070
If you twitch a muscle, I'll kill her.

01:42.654 --> 01:46.032
Isn't she one of Shuro's retainers?

01:46.533 --> 01:48.827
Was she following us this whole time?

01:49.661 --> 01:50.578
You.

01:50.662 --> 01:52.163
Undo these spells.

01:52.247 --> 01:53.081
Huh?

01:53.164 --> 01:55.166
The spells I'm under!

01:55.250 --> 01:56.334
Get to it!

01:56.417 --> 01:59.212
W-What kind of spells are you under?

01:59.295 --> 02:00.839
Can't you tell by looking?

02:00.922 --> 02:03.133
You wield black magic, don't you?

02:03.216 --> 02:05.093
At least clue me in
on what they're cast on

02:05.176 --> 02:07.345
and what kind of magic they are.

02:09.430 --> 02:12.100
There are two types of spells on me.

02:12.183 --> 02:14.227
One's on my neck.

02:14.310 --> 02:15.687
And the other...

02:15.770 --> 02:16.604
Huh?

02:20.066 --> 02:21.401
Is all over my body.

02:22.944 --> 02:25.572
Is she a beast-man?

02:25.655 --> 02:26.614
Yeah.

02:26.698 --> 02:28.741
I've seen one a long time ago.

02:28.825 --> 02:31.744
An engineered beast-man.

02:31.828 --> 02:35.582
Apparently, they're made with black magic,
mixing human and beast souls together.

02:37.584 --> 02:40.336
Fine. I'll do what I can.

02:42.172 --> 02:43.256
This...

02:43.840 --> 02:45.967
looks like it's written
in the Eastern script.

02:46.467 --> 02:47.594
What kind of spells are they?

02:48.094 --> 02:49.971
Can't you tell by looking?

02:50.054 --> 02:53.683
They activate when the spellcaster
goes without touching them for a while.

02:53.766 --> 02:56.519
Is the spellcaster the one called Maizuru?

02:56.603 --> 02:58.354
How much time do you have left?

02:58.438 --> 03:00.481
What happens when you run out of time?

03:00.565 --> 03:01.441
Who knows?

03:01.524 --> 03:03.151
You might want to hurry.

03:03.234 --> 03:05.778
You don't want to die with me, do you?

03:06.613 --> 03:08.823
I'll let you go once you undo the spells.

03:10.408 --> 03:12.493
<i>The writing is peculiar.</i>

03:12.577 --> 03:14.370
<i>But I have a feeling I can undo them.</i>

03:14.454 --> 03:15.496
Hey, you brat.

03:15.580 --> 03:16.414
Huh?

03:16.497 --> 03:17.874
Fetch me something to eat.

03:24.923 --> 03:26.841
FIELD RATION PELLET

03:28.468 --> 03:31.512
When's the last time
you had something to eat?

03:32.055 --> 03:35.016
If you shovel it in that fast,
you'll choke.

03:35.099 --> 03:36.226
Shut up.

03:36.309 --> 03:38.102
I'll prepare something hot for you.

03:38.186 --> 03:39.604
Hey! Did I say you could move?

03:39.687 --> 03:40.521
Whoa!

03:40.605 --> 03:42.232
Don't underestimate--

03:44.609 --> 03:47.570
You need something to moisten your throat.

03:47.654 --> 03:49.530
I'll fix you something. That's all.

03:49.614 --> 03:52.575
If you try
to feed me monsters, I'll kill you.

03:53.451 --> 03:54.410
Deal.

03:57.247 --> 04:01.251
I'm pretty sure I picked up some mushrooms
around where the Dryads were.

04:02.543 --> 04:05.129
<i>They're starting to sprout
leg-like things.</i>

04:05.880 --> 04:08.299
<i>Must be my imagination.</i>

04:08.883 --> 04:11.344
<i>I'll set my pot on the magic circle,</i>

04:11.427 --> 04:15.181
<i>melt some butter,
sauté some garlic,</i>

04:15.265 --> 04:16.391
<i>and toss in the rice.</i>

04:16.891 --> 04:19.394
<i>Then I'll add
the mushrooms and seasonings,</i>

04:19.477 --> 04:21.980
<i>pour in some water,
and let it stew for a bit.</i>

04:28.486 --> 04:33.908
<i>The fact that this is all I can make
makes me feel useless and pathetic.</i>

04:33.992 --> 04:38.413
<i>At any rate, I can't stand the idea
of young ones going hungry.</i>

04:38.496 --> 04:39.414
<i>But at least,</i>

04:40.081 --> 04:41.666
I can throw in some cheese.

04:42.250 --> 04:43.501
It's done.

04:43.584 --> 04:46.170
RISOTTO WITH MUSHROOMS FROM A GRAVEYARD
AND CHEESE FROM ORCS

04:46.754 --> 04:48.131
I'll put it here.

04:48.214 --> 04:49.841
You think I'd eat that?

05:02.353 --> 05:03.438
<i>This kid...</i>

05:04.022 --> 05:06.190
<i>Her table manners</i>

05:06.274 --> 05:07.483
<i>are terrible!</i>

05:08.526 --> 05:09.694
Give me more!

05:10.278 --> 05:13.489
Is etiquette different
in the East or something?

05:13.573 --> 05:16.784
We never saw Shuro eating like that.

05:17.785 --> 05:19.704
She simply had a poor upbringing.

05:20.288 --> 05:21.748
Guess that's unfamiliar to you.

05:28.838 --> 05:29.756
- Huh?
- Huh?

05:36.179 --> 05:37.597
Why did you do that?

05:37.680 --> 05:38.890
I hate mushrooms.

05:38.973 --> 05:40.016
<i>She's picky!</i>

05:40.099 --> 05:42.143
<i>This has never happened before.</i>

05:42.226 --> 05:43.144
<i>Senshi...</i>

05:45.688 --> 05:46.773
Your spoon.

05:47.482 --> 05:50.026
Hold your spoon properly.

05:50.109 --> 05:50.985
Hey!

05:51.069 --> 05:52.987
If you come any closer, I'll kill you!

05:53.071 --> 05:57.742
Hold your spoon the right way
and pick up what you threw on the floor.

05:57.825 --> 05:59.494
- What'd you say?
- Hey!

05:59.577 --> 06:00.620
Don't!

06:01.329 --> 06:03.247
It's risky to move
when I'm undoing your spell!

06:16.803 --> 06:19.097
Hold your spoon like this.

06:19.180 --> 06:20.807
W-Who cares how I hold it?

06:20.890 --> 06:23.226
This way is easier for me!

06:23.309 --> 06:25.019
I'm not surprised.

06:25.103 --> 06:28.481
Having someone force you to hold a spoon
in an unfamiliar way must be annoying.

06:28.564 --> 06:29.398
However--

06:29.482 --> 06:30.733
Senshi, behind you!

06:33.903 --> 06:35.029
Huh?

06:36.072 --> 06:37.115
<i>I didn't feel anything.</i>

06:38.574 --> 06:39.617
<i>Is this paper?</i>

06:39.700 --> 06:41.744
Senshi, watch out!

06:45.206 --> 06:49.669
That's a carving knife,
a type of knife used for cutting meat.

06:50.211 --> 06:54.132
It's got a long, sharp blade
that can look pretty intimidating,

06:54.215 --> 06:56.134
but it's thin and delicate.

06:56.217 --> 07:00.513
If you wave it around like that,
what do you think is going to happen?

07:00.596 --> 07:01.472
Senshi!

07:11.858 --> 07:15.069
Just like that, you might not get
the most out of your tool,

07:15.153 --> 07:17.780
leaving yourself at a disadvantage.

07:24.745 --> 07:25.580
Senshi!

07:25.663 --> 07:27.081
Now, Laios!

07:35.506 --> 07:38.176
Are you hurt, cat girl?

07:39.218 --> 07:41.679
I'm sorry for giving you a fright.

07:41.762 --> 07:42.597
However,

07:42.680 --> 07:47.101
there are right
and wrong ways to hold a tool.

07:47.185 --> 07:49.562
I want you to think about
why that's the case.

07:49.645 --> 07:52.648
And why you shouldn't move
while a spell's being undone.

07:53.232 --> 07:56.319
If the spells had been nastier,
who knows what might've happened.

07:57.945 --> 08:00.448
The food's gone cold.

08:00.531 --> 08:02.116
I'll reheat it quick.

08:04.535 --> 08:05.369
So?

08:05.453 --> 08:07.705
Why were you coming after us?

08:08.956 --> 08:13.669
All this time, I've been looking for a way
to break the curses on my body.

08:15.713 --> 08:18.758
Turns out, these curses
were placed by black magic.

08:18.841 --> 08:22.011
But I could never find anyone
who could wield black magic.

08:22.887 --> 08:25.473
Until I crossed paths with that long-ears.

08:25.556 --> 08:28.226
Black, I mean ancient magic
comes in all sorts.

08:28.309 --> 08:30.853
My research is mainly about
drawing energy from another dimension--

08:30.937 --> 08:31.771
Don't give me that!

08:31.854 --> 08:34.023
I know you can do it!

08:34.106 --> 08:36.651
I mean, you've done it before!

08:36.734 --> 08:40.196
<i>You wielded black magic
to create that eerie half-beast creature!</i>

08:41.656 --> 08:44.992
And you're all
trekking through this dungeon

08:45.076 --> 08:46.702
to break the curse on that woman, right?

08:46.786 --> 08:49.914
That means you know how to break curses!

08:49.997 --> 08:52.416
In that case, you can free me too!

08:53.000 --> 08:56.587
Get rid of this beast's soul
that's possessing me!

08:59.090 --> 09:00.132
I'm sorry.

09:00.716 --> 09:03.261
There's nothing I can do about that.

09:04.095 --> 09:05.179
What?

09:05.763 --> 09:08.140
<i>There's a lot we don't know
about the soul.</i>

09:08.724 --> 09:10.434
<i>But it's often likened to an egg.</i>

09:11.185 --> 09:14.146
<i>Normally, it's nestled inside
a shell we call flesh,</i>

09:14.230 --> 09:16.816
<i>but once the flesh is broken,
the insides spill out</i>

09:16.899 --> 09:18.401
<i>and can't be put back again.</i>

09:19.777 --> 09:21.571
<i>This dungeon is under a spell</i>

09:21.654 --> 09:24.407
<i>that forms a tough membrane
beneath the shell,</i>

09:24.949 --> 09:27.034
<i>keeping the soul inside
even when the body is damaged.</i>

09:28.077 --> 09:33.291
At the moment, you and Falin
have got two eggs inside one shell.

09:34.542 --> 09:36.627
And once mixed together,

09:36.711 --> 09:38.879
those souls can never go back
to their original form.

09:40.047 --> 09:43.676
<i>I knew that, but hearing it
laid out like that hits differently.</i>

09:44.302 --> 09:45.761
What?

09:45.845 --> 09:50.224
If that's the case,
why press on with your journey?

09:52.935 --> 09:56.439
One reason is
we can't just let my sister run wild.

09:56.522 --> 09:59.191
She might kill the next adventurer
she crosses paths with.

09:59.859 --> 10:01.110
Or get herself killed by them.

10:01.944 --> 10:03.779
We want to do something
before that happens.

10:04.405 --> 10:07.116
And if we return to the surface now,

10:07.199 --> 10:09.368
we'll be apprehended
for dabbling in black magic.

10:09.452 --> 10:12.580
Shuro will likely tell the Lord
of the Island about this incident.

10:13.456 --> 10:14.749
But...

10:15.333 --> 10:18.127
Does this mean I'm stuck like this?

10:18.210 --> 10:20.087
No, listen to me!

10:20.171 --> 10:24.008
I know this might sound weird,
but I'm honestly glad to have met you.

10:24.091 --> 10:26.344
I'm not sure what kind of monster
you're mixed with,

10:26.427 --> 10:28.846
but your behavior is just like a human's.

10:28.929 --> 10:30.765
And you're not out for blood either.

10:31.349 --> 10:34.935
So, maybe even Falin,
once she's free from the dungeon's grip,

10:35.019 --> 10:37.521
might be able to reclaim her true self.

10:38.147 --> 10:41.275
Just realizing that makes me

10:41.359 --> 10:43.569
so very happy right now.

10:44.236 --> 10:45.279
Here.

10:45.863 --> 10:49.116
Maybe things didn't unfold
exactly as you'd hoped,

10:49.200 --> 10:51.077
but why not look at it
from a positive angle,

10:51.160 --> 10:52.828
like it was fate at work?

10:53.371 --> 10:55.039
The lord of the dungeon

10:55.122 --> 10:58.125
is way more skilled
with ancient magic than I am.

10:58.626 --> 11:03.798
He might have some insights
on how to separate souls.

11:03.881 --> 11:04.757
Hold up.

11:04.840 --> 11:07.051
Are you trying to recruit me?

11:07.134 --> 11:10.513
Either way, you can't make it back
to the surface by yourself.

11:10.596 --> 11:13.182
Was your name Asebi or something?

11:13.265 --> 11:15.226
That's just the name I go by.

11:15.309 --> 11:16.227
Then...

11:16.310 --> 11:17.311
It's Izutsumi.

11:17.395 --> 11:19.271
My name is Izutsumi.

11:19.355 --> 11:20.439
Don't forget.

11:31.158 --> 11:34.453
Laios, how much longer are you going
to keep living like this?

11:35.037 --> 11:35.871
Father.

11:35.955 --> 11:38.082
It's about time
you started living a proper life.

11:38.165 --> 11:41.961
I didn't let you go out there
just so you could go off slaying dragons.

11:42.044 --> 11:43.587
Come back to the village!

11:44.171 --> 11:45.423
But Falin's still...

11:45.506 --> 11:47.299
Forget about her.

11:47.800 --> 11:51.303
Do you really believe someone like you
can make it out there

11:51.804 --> 11:54.807
when you ran away from both school
and the army because you couldn't fit in?

11:55.808 --> 11:58.310
You don't even have the knack
for exploring the dungeon.

11:58.811 --> 12:00.646
Just like back when you were gold-peeling,

12:00.729 --> 12:03.732
your comrades will deceive you
and take credit for your achievements.

12:04.316 --> 12:06.735
Because you're clueless
when it comes to reading people.

12:07.319 --> 12:08.988
It was the same with me.

12:09.071 --> 12:12.158
You believed we were close friends,

12:12.241 --> 12:13.951
but I've always loathed--

12:14.034 --> 12:14.994
Would you let that go?

12:15.077 --> 12:16.662
We've already talked it out.

12:16.745 --> 12:18.372
Wait, hang on.

12:18.456 --> 12:20.875
<i>Why are my parents here?</i>

12:20.958 --> 12:23.127
<i>I haven't seen them in over a decade.</i>

12:23.210 --> 12:25.004
<i>And where am I?</i>

12:25.087 --> 12:26.630
<i>What was I up to?</i>

12:26.714 --> 12:28.215
<i>I think I was...</i>

12:31.719 --> 12:33.888
<i>Lately, Marcille</i>

12:34.472 --> 12:36.682
<i>seemed kind of worn out.</i>

12:37.475 --> 12:40.519
Marcille, we'll take care
of keeping watch tonight.

12:40.603 --> 12:41.729
You rest.

12:41.812 --> 12:43.147
Huh? But why?

12:43.230 --> 12:44.398
Don't worry about me.

12:44.482 --> 12:46.567
Come on. Just rest.

12:46.650 --> 12:47.485
Hey!

12:47.568 --> 12:49.403
Ugh, what are you doing?!

12:49.987 --> 12:52.239
I'm not that tired, you know.

12:52.323 --> 12:54.033
I'll be up in a bit.

12:54.116 --> 12:55.743
I can't be the only one to...

12:56.368 --> 13:00.748
<i>But before long, her quiet breathing
turned into distressed groans.</i>

13:01.499 --> 13:03.834
What's the matter, Marcille?

13:03.918 --> 13:05.461
This isn't something to take lightly.

13:05.544 --> 13:06.545
Is it a monster?

13:06.629 --> 13:08.797
Yeah, I think it's a Nightmare.

13:08.881 --> 13:11.967
<i>They prey on humans in their sleep,
inflicting them with nightmares,</i>

13:12.051 --> 13:13.552
<i>and feed on their emotions.</i>

13:14.136 --> 13:17.139
If this goes on,
Marcille will weaken and die.

13:17.640 --> 13:19.350
Wake up, Marcille!

13:19.433 --> 13:22.102
Don't. If you force her awake,
you'll harm her soul.

13:23.354 --> 13:27.566
When Shuro was possessed before,
Falin entered his dreams to rescue him.

13:28.275 --> 13:30.069
Let's try that.

13:30.152 --> 13:32.363
You're going to enter her dream?

13:32.446 --> 13:35.324
Someone needs
to help her realize she's dreaming.

13:35.407 --> 13:38.911
Use the dreamer as a pillow and...

13:46.210 --> 13:49.338
<i>Right. I was trying to help Marcille.</i>

13:50.047 --> 13:51.924
I'm inside my own dream!

13:52.925 --> 13:55.094
The Nightmare got an easy bite out of me.

13:55.177 --> 13:56.470
It's always like this.

13:56.554 --> 13:58.722
They sure know how to hit where it hurts!

13:59.306 --> 14:02.351
But now that I know it's just a dream,
I've got the upper hand.

14:02.434 --> 14:05.271
Come forth, my mightiest servant!

14:10.192 --> 14:13.237
<i>Now, I need to enter Marcille's dream.</i>

14:14.446 --> 14:16.365
Since she's serving
as my pillow right now,

14:16.866 --> 14:19.451
I'll have to dig down.

14:23.539 --> 14:25.249
This is the beauty of dreams.

14:25.332 --> 14:27.084
This only works inside
your own dream, though.

14:32.840 --> 14:33.799
That was a close one.

14:34.383 --> 14:36.427
That fall almost jolted me awake.

14:37.720 --> 14:40.764
So this is what
Marcille's dream looks like.

14:42.266 --> 14:43.893
Pretty cool.

14:43.976 --> 14:45.144
Is someone there?

14:45.644 --> 14:47.104
What are you doing?

14:47.688 --> 14:49.940
This place is dangerous.
You need to get out fast.

14:51.567 --> 14:52.818
Marcille?

14:52.902 --> 14:54.737
W-Who are you?

14:54.820 --> 14:56.322
It's me, Laios!

14:56.405 --> 14:58.824
And we're inside your dream!

14:58.908 --> 15:01.827
You need to wake up and...

15:01.911 --> 15:02.786
A tremor?

15:03.954 --> 15:05.414
It's coming!

15:05.497 --> 15:07.416
W-We need to run!

15:07.499 --> 15:08.584
What's coming?

15:08.667 --> 15:09.960
Just follow me!

15:11.045 --> 15:14.214
<i>It swallowed Papa and Pipi.</i>

15:14.298 --> 15:15.799
<i>Papa and Pipi?</i>

15:16.884 --> 15:18.719
<i>A dream about being chased, huh?</i>

15:18.802 --> 15:21.305
<i>Those are pretty common, but nasty.</i>

15:22.306 --> 15:23.474
<i>I remember Falin mentioning...</i>

15:24.224 --> 15:26.894
Nightmares thrive on emotional scars.

15:27.811 --> 15:30.105
Stressful events and trauma.

15:30.189 --> 15:34.026
They trigger those memories
and give people nightmares.

15:35.110 --> 15:38.197
So all we have to do
is shield their scars.

15:38.280 --> 15:39.281
I see.

15:39.865 --> 15:40.699
But...

15:41.325 --> 15:43.285
It's dangerous, so don't try it.

15:43.369 --> 15:45.245
All right. I got it!

15:45.329 --> 15:47.623
I'll take it down for you!

15:48.207 --> 15:50.250
What are you doing? It's too risky!

15:50.334 --> 15:51.919
Don't worry.

15:52.002 --> 15:53.754
I might not seem like it,
but I'm actually...

16:05.724 --> 16:07.393
What in the world is that?

16:07.476 --> 16:09.061
How should I know?

16:09.645 --> 16:12.064
<i>Is that what Marcille's afraid of?</i>

16:12.648 --> 16:14.733
<i>It's quite a bit over the top,</i>

16:14.817 --> 16:17.319
<i>but it does look like
it'll be tough for me to take down.</i>

16:18.654 --> 16:21.657
<i>It wouldn't be a threat if she realized
this was all just a dream, though.</i>

16:22.825 --> 16:24.034
We've come far enough.

16:24.910 --> 16:26.912
Nowhere is safe.

16:27.913 --> 16:29.456
Nobody stands a chance against it.

16:31.417 --> 16:32.501
Don't worry.

16:32.584 --> 16:34.461
Let's think of a way
to take it down together.

16:35.921 --> 16:38.173
<i>What is Marcille afraid of?</i>

16:38.799 --> 16:40.592
<i>A monster, of course.</i>

16:41.427 --> 16:43.303
<i>It crawls sluggishly,</i>

16:43.387 --> 16:45.973
<i>has countless tentacles
and an insatiable hunger,</i>

16:46.515 --> 16:47.933
<i>and looks disgusting.</i>

16:48.726 --> 16:49.852
<i>Is it some kind of insect?</i>

16:49.935 --> 16:53.397
<i>But bugs that size are pretty rare.</i>

16:53.981 --> 16:55.858
<i>Bugs...</i>

16:55.941 --> 16:57.109
<i>That's it!</i>

16:57.192 --> 16:58.736
It's a Wurm!

16:58.819 --> 17:00.612
It's a Wurm from the Dragon family!

17:00.696 --> 17:03.615
Its legs and eyes have degenerated,
so it's more like a giant caterpillar.

17:03.699 --> 17:06.368
It's voracious
and devours anything living!

17:06.452 --> 17:08.370
It's weak to fire and light!

17:08.454 --> 17:10.956
Pretty classy choice!

17:11.749 --> 17:12.583
Huh?

17:14.460 --> 17:15.586
When did it...

17:16.670 --> 17:17.880
Hold on!

17:18.839 --> 17:20.758
R-Run!

17:21.300 --> 17:23.510
Did that thing touch you?

17:23.594 --> 17:25.095
Just a brush.

17:25.179 --> 17:26.013
Show me!

17:29.725 --> 17:30.642
What's this?

17:40.194 --> 17:41.028
<i>Damn.</i>

17:41.111 --> 17:42.780
<i>I frightened her even more!</i>

17:42.863 --> 17:45.032
<i>It'll only make the Nightmare stronger.</i>

17:49.369 --> 17:51.288
<i>What a potent poison.</i>

17:51.371 --> 17:53.957
<i>What happens if you die
in someone else's dream?</i>

17:54.625 --> 17:58.128
<i>No, it wants us
to feel anxious and scared.</i>

17:58.212 --> 18:00.047
<i>I have to lift Marcille's spirits.</i>

18:00.130 --> 18:01.298
Don't worry!

18:01.381 --> 18:03.509
You can use magic!

18:03.592 --> 18:06.011
You can take that thing down
all by yourself!

18:07.012 --> 18:08.055
Magic?

18:13.393 --> 18:15.354
<i>The place is getting even more unstable.</i>

18:15.437 --> 18:17.189
<i>Did I say something wrong?</i>

18:17.272 --> 18:18.315
When...

18:18.899 --> 18:22.236
When I tried to use magic to defeat it,

18:22.778 --> 18:25.405
she ended up like this.

18:26.698 --> 18:27.699
She?

18:27.783 --> 18:30.202
Wait, is that Falin?

18:30.285 --> 18:31.954
<i>I get it now.</i>

18:32.037 --> 18:34.081
<i>Marcille feels guilty
about Falin's transformation</i>

18:34.164 --> 18:36.041
<i>due to her resurrection magic.</i>

18:36.125 --> 18:38.710
<i>If she tried
to defeat that thing, it means...</i>

18:38.794 --> 18:41.296
<i>Marcille is afraid of death!</i>

18:41.797 --> 18:43.549
I-It's coming back!

18:44.174 --> 18:46.593
Running won't solve anything.

18:46.677 --> 18:48.554
You have to face it head-on.

18:48.637 --> 18:49.596
What?

18:49.680 --> 18:52.933
Don't worry.
There's nothing for you to fear!

18:53.433 --> 18:55.853
In the dungeon, even if you die,
you can come back to life.

18:55.936 --> 18:59.356
Even Falin is still alive
thanks to your resurrection magic.

18:59.439 --> 19:01.650
And you're used to seeing corpses, right?

19:01.733 --> 19:03.360
What?!

19:08.657 --> 19:10.117
It's pulling me in!

19:10.200 --> 19:11.368
No!

19:11.451 --> 19:13.120
It's only pulling me!

19:13.203 --> 19:14.705
Grab my hand!

19:18.083 --> 19:19.376
<i>It's not poison.</i>

19:19.459 --> 19:22.129
<i>I'm aging at an incredible rate.</i>

19:23.088 --> 19:24.631
W-Wait a minute, Marcille.

19:24.715 --> 19:25.924
I need to catch my breath.

19:26.967 --> 19:28.510
<i>Something's not right.</i>

19:28.594 --> 19:31.263
<i>Is there a creature capable of this?</i>

19:31.346 --> 19:33.724
<i>Maybe it's not even a creature at all.</i>

19:33.807 --> 19:36.393
So you won't come along with me either?

19:36.476 --> 19:39.354
No, I can run again after a short rest.

19:39.438 --> 19:40.272
You're lying!

19:40.355 --> 19:44.860
Everyone who ran with me gave up,
and they were all swallowed by that thing.

19:44.943 --> 19:48.363
Papa, Pipi, Falin, everyone!

19:48.447 --> 19:51.700
That's why I studied a lot of magic.

19:51.783 --> 19:55.037
But if that's what turned Falin into this,

19:55.120 --> 19:57.289
I don't know what to do.

19:58.749 --> 20:01.710
Did your father pass away young?

20:02.336 --> 20:05.422
At Papa's funeral, Mama told me

20:06.006 --> 20:09.051
<i>that I run faster than everyone else.</i>

20:09.551 --> 20:13.472
<i>That I'd have to watch
a lot of people go away.</i>

20:14.014 --> 20:16.600
By the way, is Pipi a relative of yours?

20:16.683 --> 20:17.684
Pipi's a bird.

20:17.768 --> 20:18.810
<i>I see.</i>

20:19.519 --> 20:22.606
<i>Marcille isn't afraid of death.</i>

20:22.689 --> 20:26.026
<i>She's worried that those she cares about
will pass away before her.</i>

20:32.866 --> 20:34.201
Marcille, calm down!

20:34.284 --> 20:37.204
If you're scared,
it'll just empower that thing.

20:37.287 --> 20:39.873
But what am I supposed to do?

20:39.957 --> 20:41.083
I can't do anything!

20:41.166 --> 20:42.709
No, you can!

20:42.793 --> 20:45.212
You're incredible, Marcille!

20:45.295 --> 20:47.714
I mean, just look at all these books!

20:47.798 --> 20:50.300
There was nothing like that in my dream!

20:50.801 --> 20:53.470
You've been working tirelessly
all this time!

20:53.553 --> 20:56.056
Don't lose heart. Have faith in yourself!

20:56.556 --> 20:58.350
You've got this, Marcille!

20:58.433 --> 21:00.352
No, get up!

21:00.435 --> 21:01.812
We have to run!

21:01.895 --> 21:02.980
And besides,

21:03.063 --> 21:05.732
my magic isn't fully developed!

21:05.816 --> 21:08.235
<i>If I had the same book he does,</i>

21:08.860 --> 21:11.530
<i>I could use magic more effectively, but...</i>

21:11.613 --> 21:13.865
Then wish for it!

21:13.949 --> 21:16.618
If you wish hard enough,
you can accomplish anything!

21:16.702 --> 21:19.746
Don't be afraid!
You can do better next time!

21:19.830 --> 21:21.373
Don't give up!

21:21.957 --> 21:24.626
No!

21:24.710 --> 21:26.628
No!

21:34.594 --> 21:36.346
That's it, Marcille!

21:36.430 --> 21:37.389
Do it!

21:48.025 --> 21:51.236
That's how you use it?!

21:55.073 --> 21:56.325
You're awake.

21:56.408 --> 21:58.243
You were both groaning in your sleep.

21:58.327 --> 21:59.369
Are you okay?

21:59.453 --> 22:01.872
I don't really remember.

22:01.955 --> 22:04.499
It was an exhausting dream, though.

22:09.212 --> 22:10.213
She's falling back asleep!

22:10.297 --> 22:12.382
No! Wake up, Marcille!

22:13.800 --> 22:14.760
My dream?

22:15.344 --> 22:16.636
I don't remember much.

22:16.720 --> 22:19.598
But I think it was a fun one.

22:19.681 --> 22:21.308
Looks like it worked.

22:21.391 --> 22:22.893
Did something happen?

22:22.976 --> 22:24.519
Pass me your pillow.

22:24.603 --> 22:25.520
Huh?

22:28.774 --> 22:29.608
What are those?

22:29.691 --> 22:31.026
Nightmares.

22:31.109 --> 22:34.696
They hide in people's pillows
and give them bad dreams.

22:35.363 --> 22:37.574
There are so many of them.

22:37.657 --> 22:39.868
They must have been
nesting in your pillow for a while.

22:39.951 --> 22:40.786
No way!

22:40.869 --> 22:42.662
Senshi, are these edible?

22:42.746 --> 22:44.748
I've always been curious
about their flavor.

22:44.831 --> 22:46.208
Yes, of course.

22:47.250 --> 22:49.169
First, let's clean the gunk off.

22:50.754 --> 22:53.048
If you soak them in hot water like this...

22:54.257 --> 22:57.135
Nightmares, also known as Shen,

22:57.219 --> 22:59.012
are actually related to Dragons.

22:59.096 --> 23:01.056
If you look closely,
they're a bit Dragon-like.

23:01.139 --> 23:02.432
You're kidding me.

23:02.516 --> 23:06.269
<i>Place the Nightmares in melted butter,</i>

23:06.353 --> 23:08.647
<i>add some wine, and cover with a lid.</i>

23:12.025 --> 23:15.195
<i>Finally, drizzle a bit
of soy sauce over them,</i>

23:15.278 --> 23:16.696
and it's done.

23:19.282 --> 23:20.283
What's this?

23:21.368 --> 23:22.452
That's me!

23:23.036 --> 23:26.039
The dream that the Nightmares devoured
turned into a mirage.

23:26.123 --> 23:28.708
It's coming back to me.

23:28.792 --> 23:29.751
Right,

23:29.835 --> 23:31.837
I was running from something

23:31.920 --> 23:33.505
<i>when a dog appeared.</i>

23:34.464 --> 23:37.968
And we went on a treasure hunt together.

23:38.051 --> 23:40.303
It was such a fun dream!

23:40.387 --> 23:42.305
The dog seems a bit scruffy.

23:42.389 --> 23:43.974
It looks dumb.

23:44.558 --> 23:45.684
What's wrong, Laios?

23:46.226 --> 23:49.855
I remember it being a silver wolf, but...

23:49.938 --> 23:51.189
Never mind.

23:51.273 --> 23:54.192
I'm glad if I helped in creating
a fun dream for her.

25:30.121 --> 25:31.957
Subtitle translation by: Ai Matsuoka
